      "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe kept CI venv lives at `/opt/sglang-ci-py3.12`, inside the runner's own filesystem. The sourcem 5090 runners are now k3s pods, and a pod's filesystem lives in k3s's containerd store on the node's **root drive**. Two of those nodes have budget consumer root drives (Kingston NV3, WD Blue SN5000), and copying several GB of packages into the venv there took minutes instead of under a second. \"Install dependencies\" timed out at 20 minutes, and uv's shared-cache lock timed out after 300 s for the runners queued behind it.\n\nFor the same install step, `Installed 27 packages` took **0.36 s** on sourcem-node-4, whose runners keep their filesystem on the `/data` RAID, and **2 min 05 s** on sourcem-node-2, a k3s pod on a Kingston NV3 root drive.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `ci_install_dependency.sh` uses `SGLANG_CI_KEPT_VENV_DIR` for the kept venv when it's set, and creates its parent directory. **Unset keeps today's `/opt/sglang-ci-py3.12`**, so every other runner is unaffected.\n- The variable is deliberately not `SGLANG_CI_VENV_PATH`: `ci_cleanup_venv.sh` deletes that path after every job.\n\nThe runner side, mounting a per-runner `/data` directory and setting this variable on the sourcem pods, is a separate change in the platform repo. Until it lands, nothing sets the variable.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `bash -n` passes.\n- Checked the path resolution with the variable unset (`/opt/sglang-ci-py3.12`) and set (the given directory).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40150408150](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40150408150)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40150408183](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40150408183)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40150408144](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40150408144)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
